-- title:
--   Γ'-invariant pull-back of a section to Drinfeld's upper half plane
-- statement:
--   The setting is a Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation datum, described binder by binder.
--
--   **The base ring.** A prime $r$; a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi \in \mathcal O$, the hypothesis that $\mathcal O$ is complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, that the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and that $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (absolute unramifiedness); a field $K_0$ of characteristic zero which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The unramified extension.** A commutative domain $Onr$ of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$ of $Onr$, subject to: `hOnr_complete`, $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$; `hOnr_max`, that ideal is maximal; `hOnr_alg`, every $x \in Onr$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$; `hOnr_closed`, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$; and `hFr`, $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$.
--
--   **The determinant valuation.** A monoid homomorphism $v\!\det : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively), characterised by `hvdet`: $v\!\det(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The group.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma \le G$, with `hcent`: some $z \in \Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix and $v\!\det(\sigma z) = 2$; `hodd`: some $w \in \Gamma$ has $v\!\det(\sigma w) = 1$; and a subgroup $\Gamma' \le G$ characterised elementwise by `hΓ'`: $x \in \Gamma'$ iff $x \in \Gamma$ and $v\!\det(\sigma x)$ is even. Further, a homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with `hρ`: $\rho g$ is the class of $\sigma g$; `hdisc`: for every vertex $v$ of the Bruhat–Tits lattice tree of $(\mathcal O, K_0)$ (homothety classes of full lattices in $K_0^2$) the set of elements of $\rho(\Gamma')$ fixing $v$ is finite; and `hcocpt`: there is a finite set $S$ of vertices such that every vertex is carried into $S$ by some element of $\rho(\Gamma')$.
--
--   **The coarse quotient.** A scheme $\mathcal X$ and a proper flat morphism $f : \mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. Write $\mathcal F$ for the functor $B \mapsto (Onr \to_{\mathcal O} B) \times \Omega(B)$ on $\mathcal O$-algebras, where $\Omega(B)$ is the set of Deligne data over $B$: families assigning to each full lattice $M \subset K_0^2$ a $B$-submodule $\mathrm{line}(M)$ of $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$ with invertible quotient, compatible with lattice inclusions, equivariant for scalar homotheties, and satisfying the nondegeneracy condition of `DeligneDatum` at every prime of $B$; and write $\mathcal X^{\mathrm{nilp}}(B) = \{\varphi : \operatorname{Spec} B \to \mathcal X \mid \varphi$ followed by $f$ is the structure map $\operatorname{Spec} B \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O\}$. A family $\Theta$ of maps $\mathcal F(B) \to \mathcal X^{\mathrm{nilp}}(B)$, defined for all $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, subject to: `hΘnat`, naturality in $B$ along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps; `hΘinv`, $\Theta$ is constant on twisted $\Gamma$-orbits, i.e. $\Theta(x') = \Theta(x)$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma$ and `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` holds for $\sigma\gamma$ and $x, x'$, which means that the $Onr$-component of $x'$ is the $Fr^{-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma)}$-twist of that of $x$ and the Deligne datum of $x'$ is the pull-back of that of $x$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$; `hΘfib`, for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi : Onr \to_{\mathcal O} k$, every element of $\mathcal X^{\mathrm{nilp}}(k)$ is $\Theta(\psi, P)$ for some Deligne datum $P$, and $\Theta(\psi,P) = \Theta(\psi,P')$ if and only if some $\gamma \in \Gamma$ twistedly carries $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi,P')$; and `hΘuniv`, the universal property: for every scheme $T$ with a morphism $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and every family $\rho'$ of maps $\mathcal F(B) \to T^{\mathrm{nilp}}(B)$ which is natural in $B$ and constant on twisted $\Gamma$-orbits, there exists a family $u$ of maps $\mathcal X^{\mathrm{nilp}}(B) \to T^{\mathrm{nilp}}(B)$, natural in $B$, with $u \circ \Theta = \rho'$, and any other such natural family $u'$ satisfying $u' \circ \Theta = \rho'$ agrees with $u$ on every $\mathcal X^{\mathrm{nilp}}(B)$.
--
--   **The analytic frame.** A field $C$ with a $K_0$-algebra structure, a valuation $v$ on $C$ with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$, $C$ complete and algebraically closed; a commutative ring $R$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $C$ an $R$-algebra and the evident scalar towers over $\mathcal O$; a pseudo-uniformizer $\varpi$, that is an element $\varpi \in K_0$ with $0 < v(\varpi) < 1$ in $C$ and such that for every $a \in K_0^{\times}$ some power $v(\varpi)^{N}$ bounds $v(a)$ from below and $v(\varpi)^{-N}$ bounds it from above; and `hF : IsAdicFrame π ϖ R`, which asserts that $\pi$ is irreducible, that $R \to C$ is injective with image exactly $\{c : v(c) \le 1\}$, that $R$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that $\{a \in K_0 : v(a) \le 1\}$ is the image of $\mathcal O$, that the image of $K_0$ in $C$ is closed, and that $\pi$ and $\varpi$ have the same image in $C$. Further: an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi_0 : Onr \to R$; `hrk`, for all $x, y \in C$ with $v(x) < 1$ and $y \neq 0$ there is $n$ with $v(x)^{n} \le v(y)$; `hval`, for every $\varepsilon \in \Gamma_0 \setminus \{0\}$ there is $y \neq 0$ in $C$ with $v(y) \le \varepsilon$; `hex : Omega.IsExhausted ϖ`, every point of the Drinfeld upper half plane $\Omega_C = C \setminus \mathrm{im}(K_0)$ lies in one of the affinoids $\{z : v(z) \le v(\varpi)^{-n}$ and $v(z - a) \ge v(\varpi)^{n}$ for all $a \in K_0$ with $v(a) \le v(\varpi)^{-n}\}$; and the assumption that the ring of functions on $\Omega_C$ holomorphic on every such affinoid is a domain.
--
--   **The uniformisation of adic points.** Writing $\mathrm{AdicPoint}$ for the set of compatible systems $(P_n)_n$ of Deligne data $P_n$ over $R/(\pi^{n+1})$ (compatible under the transition maps), a map $\Phi$ from $\mathrm{AdicPoint}$ to the set of morphisms $p : \operatorname{Spec} R \to \mathcal X$ with $p$ followed by $f$ the structure map, together with `hΦ`, a conjunction of four clauses: (i) for every $x$ and every $n$, the reduction $\operatorname{Spec}(R/(\pi^{n+1})) \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ followed by $\Phi(x)$ equals $\Theta$ evaluated at the pair consisting of $\psi_0$ reduced modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ and $P_n$; (ii) $\Phi$ is surjective; (iii) $\Phi(x) = \Phi(x')$ if and only if $x' = x.\mathrm{act}(\sigma\gamma)$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma'$; (iv) base change to $C$, that is $p \mapsto (\operatorname{Spec} C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ followed by $p)$, is injective on these $R$-points, and every $cpt : \operatorname{Spec} C \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ arises in this way.
--
--   **The fibre over $C$.** A morphism $sC : \operatorname{Spec} C \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `hsC` identifying it with the morphism induced by $\mathcal O \to K_0 \to C$, and the assumption that the pullback $\mathcal X_C = \mathcal X \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O} \operatorname{Spec} C$ is an integral scheme.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every open subset $U$ of $\mathcal X_C$ containing the generic point of $\mathcal X_C$ and every section $s \in \mathcal O_{\mathcal X_C}(U)$, there exists a function $F : \Omega_C \to C$ on the Drinfeld upper half plane $\Omega_C = C \setminus \mathrm{im}(K_0)$ with the following two properties.
--
--   First, $F$ computes the values of $s$ along the uniformisation: for every adic point $x$ and every $z \in \Omega_C$ with $z = x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ (the unique $z \in C$ with $(z,1)$ lying in the $C$-span of the image of the standard line of $x$, and $0$ if there is no such unique $z$), and for every morphism $q : \operatorname{Spec} C \to \mathcal X_C$ whose first projection is $\operatorname{Spec} C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ followed by $\Phi(x)$ and whose second projection is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} C$, and for every witness that $q^{-1}(U)$ is all of $\operatorname{Spec} C$, the value $F(z)$ equals the element of $C$ obtained from $s$ by applying $q$ on sections over $U$, restricting along $\top \le q^{-1}(U)$ and using the isomorphism $\mathcal O_{\operatorname{Spec} C}(\operatorname{Spec} C) \cong C$; in other words $F(z)$ is the value of $s$ at the $C$-point of $\mathcal X_C$ over $\Phi(x)$.
--
--   Second, $F$ is $\Gamma'$-invariant: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma'$ and all $z, w \in \Omega_C$ with $w = \rho(\gamma)\,z$ for the Möbius action of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ on $C$ (via the one-point extension), one has $F(w) = F(z)$.
--
--   This is the function-theoretic half of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: sections of the generic fibre $\mathcal X_C$ near its generic point are transported, through the bijection between adic points of the formal upper half plane and points of $\Omega_C$, to $\Gamma'$-invariant $C$-valued functions on Drinfeld's upper half plane. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_invariant_chartwiseMeromorphic_pullback_of_cover_clearing_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_invariant_chartwiseMeromorphic_pullback_of_cover_clearing_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient), where such pull-backs are upgraded to chartwise meromorphic functions, en route to identifying the function field of $\mathcal X_C$ with the field of $\Gamma'$-invariant meromorphic functions on $\Omega_C$.
